      "name": "How does aerosol valve selection prevent nozzle clogging in spray repellents?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Standard vertical valves with mechanical breakup actuators (MBUs) use internal swirl chambers to atomize liquid streams containing hydrophobic actives and film formers into fine mist without solid precipitations. Stem orifice sizing (typically 0.013 to 0.020 inches) prevents localized crystallization during solvent flash."
      }
